WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.020
In 1869, T.

2
00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:02.240
H.

3
00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:04.570
Huxley coined a new word.

4
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.610
Agnostic: someone who believes we
cannot know whether God exists.

5
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.300
An atheist goes further, and
believes there is no God.

6
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.580
And most Humanists are
atheists or agnostics.

7
00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.790
But without God, where
do your morals come from?

8
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.680
And what happens when you die?

9
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:26.570
In this mission, you'll place theists,
atheists and agnostics on one line,

10
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.900
and meet the Humanist way of life.

11
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:33.360
Then you will weigh up a big
claim: can you be good without God?

12
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:37.690
Your mission: find out where
non-religious people say morals come from,

13
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.550
and what they believe about death.
